# Guide typography

When writing or editing guides in `content/guides/`, follow `content/guides/GUIDE-STANDARD.md`.

## Readable text uses Helvetica Neue

These render in Helvetica Neue on the site (handled by CSS, not markdown):

- Body paragraphs
- Table headers and cells (`| col | col |` pipe tables)
- Guide card descriptions on the homepage and `/guides` hub

## Keep pixel / display fonts only where specified

- **Bootzy TM**: page title, `##` section subheaders
- **NewPixel**: lead paragraph (`description` under the title)
- **Mono**: copy-paste prompt blocks

Do not try to set fonts in markdown. Use structure only.

## Tables

- Use pipe tables for comparisons, checklists, and setup pickers.
- Never put tables inside prompt blocks.
- Table copy should be plain, scannable sentences. No pixel-font styling tricks.
